  "data": {
    "body": "You hold a piece of compressible Jell-O mass \\textbf{M = 0.3 kg} with its center of mass \\textbf{h = 0.35 m} above the top of your kitchen table. You let go of the Jell-O and just before it hits the table top, its center of mass has fallen a distance, \\textbf{d = 0.29 m}. After hitting the table top, the Jell-O comes to rest such that the center of mass of the Jell-O is finally at height \\textbf{b = 0.03 m} above the table top.\n\nUse magnitude of acceleration due to gravity g = 10 $m/s^2$",
